cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PollinationPro: a browser-based platform for analysing plants, pollinators and their overlap with occurrence data"
abstract: >-
  PollinationPro is a self-contained web application that carries a study of plants and their flower
  visitors from occurrence records to a paper, in the browser, with no installation and no third-party
  libraries. It works for any crop, crop wild relative or native plant and any group of visitors. It
  gathers GBIF records by taxon and country, published plant–visitor interactions and the user's own
  presence and visit tables; cleans the records (impossible and placeholder coordinates, country and state
  centroids, swapped or unsigned coordinates, duplicates, imprecision, fossils, living collections and
  cultivated plants, decided per plant) and harmonises synonyms; maps them offline; tests spatial
  co-occurrence with Veech's exact hypergeometric model within a target-group universe, with
  false-discovery-rate adjustment, cell-size sensitivity, a nearest-neighbour Monte Carlo test and range
  overlap; analyses phenological and elevational overlap with circular statistics; compares environmental
  niches in principal-component space with Schoener's D, Warren's I and the equivalency and similarity
  tests, reading the user's GeoTIFF or ASCII layers; estimates potential distributions and the spatial
  mismatch between a plant and its potential visitors, now and under future climates; and describes the
  interaction network (connectance, NODF, H2', d', modularity, strength, null models, sampling
  completeness). It writes a report whose methods are drawn from what was actually run.
type: software
